# {{.project_name}}

Prompt application generated from the AAI platform template (`prompt-app`):
governed prompt lifecycle with pinned-version evaluation and gated alias
promotion.

## Local setup

Before generation, complete the platform's developer onboarding checklist.
Then run the generated preflight and setup:

```bash
python3.12 scripts/setup_dev.py
make check
```

Run `make help` for individual development, evaluation, and bundle targets.

Use `python3.12 scripts/setup_dev.py --check-only` to verify tools,
authentication, SDK volume access, and compute-policy visibility without
installing anything. The setup never grants permissions or creates cloud
resources.

Replace every `replace-with-*` value in `aai-platform.yml` before running a
provider integration.

## Prompt lifecycle

1. Edit `prompts/system_prompt.json` — the versioned prompt source.
2. Register a new immutable version: `python scripts/register_prompt.py`
   (also points the `development` alias at it).
3. Configure the approved `judge-model`, then gate the version:
   `python evals/evaluate.py` — explicitly routed LLM judges (Correctness,
   RelevanceToQuery, Safety) against `evals/data/release_cases.json` with the
   thresholds in `evals/gate_config.json`; evaluation always pins an exact
   version, never an alias. After a released run passes, refresh the
   regression baseline with `--update-baseline`.
   After case changes merge, register the ground truth in Unity Catalog:
   `python scripts/sync_dataset.py` — evaluation runs link the dataset
   by name.
4. Promote only after the gate passes:
   `python scripts/promote_prompt.py --version <n> --to validation`, then
   `--to production` at release approval. Production deploys load the
   `production` alias — promotion must happen before the first prod deploy.
5. Deploy the evaluation job: `databricks bundle validate -t dev` then
   `databricks bundle deploy -t dev`.

Prompt changes are application releases: record them, evaluate them, and
promote them deliberately. Pull-request CI runs only the deterministic
checks in `evals/offline_checks.py` — it never holds credentials.

The platform team must onboard this repository (main-branch federated
credential, Databricks service principal, constrained compute permission,
non-secret repository variables) before the deploy workflow is enabled. The
Unity Catalog prompt registry (Beta) must be enabled in the workspace.
